 ### When should I book the exam?
 
-Book when your readiness score is stable and above 80, and you have covered every domain at least once. Consistent strong performance under timed conditions is a better signal than one high score.
+Book when your Readiness Score is stable and above 80, and you have covered every domain at least once. Consistent strong performance under timed conditions is a better signal than one high score.
 
 ### How long is the exam?
 
-**180 minutes** for 75 questions (65 scored, 10 unscored). That averages to roughly 2 minutes and 16 seconds per question. Scenario-heavy questions with long context may take longer, so keep an eye on the clock. Answer every question; the unscored ones are indistinguishable from scored ones.
+The exam duration is **180 minutes** for 75 questions (65 scored, 10 unscored). That averages to roughly 2 minutes and 16 seconds per question. Scenario-heavy questions with long context may take longer, so keep an eye on the clock. Answer every question; the unscored ones are indistinguishable from scored ones.
 
 ### What is the passing score?
 
-**750 out of 1000.** AWS uses scaled scoring. The raw number of correct answers needed varies slightly between exam versions. Do not try to calculate how many questions you can afford to miss.
